1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,320
Portal Accessibility Checker for JSM. A Forge app that helps a service
desk team check what its customer portal exposes, against WCAG 2.2 AA.

2
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:13,000
This video is a real screen capture, recorded on
10 November 2026 against the production build, version 2.8.0.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,360
Here is the app inside the Jira administration area of the site.
Settings, then Apps, then Portal Accessibility Checker for JSM.

4
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:29,000
Jira renders this page only for a signed-in administrator: there is no public
URL, and the server checks the administrator permission before any read.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,880
This is the page. Two optional fields, left empty here:
the greyed text is the app's placeholder, not real data.

6
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:43,120
The app's own note says the answer shows the value masked, never in clear text.
Two buttons. “Run the scan” reads your own site through the site's REST API.

7
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:47,000
“Run the demo scan” runs the same engine on the app's bundled sample data.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:56,080
Here the demo scan has just run. 23 findings,
9 of them to be checked by a human. Mode: demo.

9
00:00:56,080 --> 00:01:05,000
The scan replays the app's own fixtures: it
reads no data from the site and writes nothing.

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:16,080
Every line is a WCAG 2.2 criterion, the level,
where it was found and what the app proposes.

11
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:29,000
The last column says whether a human has to check it:
an automatic check is never a verdict of conformance.

12
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:47,000
“Export the findings” produces the same list as a CSV, with the criterion, the
level, the source, the location, the message and whether a human has to check it.

13
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:58,800
And the app states its own limits. Contrast, reading order and visible labels
are not checkable through the REST API, so the app does not rule on them.

14
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:05,000
A finding is an alert to be checked by a human, never a verdict of conformance.

15
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Portal Accessibility Checker for JSM. Production version 2.8.0, read-only, Atlassian
Cloud, no external service. The code is public, under the MIT licence, on GitHub.
